\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces One MST layer, read bottom to top. Colour encodes width and nothing else: blue operates at $D$, orange at $d=D/N$. The $N$ streams run ordinary transformer sublayers in parallel and never read each other's channels; the coupling is the only path between them, and everything they exchange passes through the single $d$-vector $a$. Grey lines are residual connections, which carry each stream past the coupling unchanged.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:arch}{{2}{4}{One MST layer, read bottom to top. Colour encodes width and nothing else: blue operates at $\dmodel $, orange at $\dsub =\dmodel /\nsub $. The $\nsub $ streams run ordinary transformer sublayers in parallel and never read each other's channels; the coupling is the only path between them, and everything they exchange passes through the single $\dsub $-vector $a$. Grey lines are residual connections, which carry each stream past the coupling unchanged}{figure.2}{}}
